y be flooded. Storm\ndrains and ditches may become clogged with debris.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Flooding is likely with additional rounds of showers and\nthunderstorms expected through Thursday night. The potential for\nflooding impacts continues into Friday.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","ends":"2026-10-23T12:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Southwest San Juan Mountains; Four Corners/Upper Dolores River; Animas River Basin; San Juan River Basin; Southeast Utah; Arches/Grand Flat; La Sal and Abajo Mountains; Canyonlands/Natural Bridges","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.960b0b92aef0a7c98e49f29c8c75ee65657db12f.002.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-22T19:15:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 221915 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 115 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Widespread rain continues through early Friday. - Flooding/Flash Flooding is likely across portions of southwest Colorado and southeast Utah. - Modeled responses suggest several rivers reaching bankfull or higher at river forecast points across southwest C","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-22T18:58:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... This is an automatically generated forecast with no discussion. The normal Fire Weather Forecast will resume in its entirety in the spring. ...GUSTY ERRATIC WINDS CAN BE EXPECTED NEAR ANY SHOWERS OR THUNDERSTORMS... ...THE SMOKE DATA IS CALCULATED FROM AN AVERAGE AT 6000 FEET MSL... COZ200-231100- Little Snake Forecast Area- 1258 PM MDT Thu Oct 22 2026","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"mnc01","station_name":"Mancos","distance_km":5.1,"soil_temp_5cm_f":54.01,"soil_temp_15cm_f":53.4,"soil_m